# Byte-exact specification artifacts. Their published SHA-256 digests are
# load-bearing: four recorded independent-verification runs, the
# verification kit's pinned fetch manifest, the CI regeneration gates,
# and the in-repo digest-pin test all compare exact bytes. A checkout
# that converts line endings (Windows runners default to autocrlf=true)
# is corruption of the artifact, so conversion is disabled for them.
docs/specs/pala-1/PALA-1.md -text
docs/specs/pala-1/profiles/robotics.md -text
docs/specs/pala-1/profiles/inference.md -text
docs/specs/pala-1/test-vectors.json -text
docs/specs/pala-1/profiles/inference-vectors.json -text
# POSIX shell must stay LF to execute at all.
docs/specs/pala-1/verification-kit/fetch-inputs.sh -text
# Generated alongside the core vectors and compared byte-for-byte by the
# regeneration gates; the SCITT statement vectors' digests are pinned in the
# bridge runs (B3 recorded a CRLF checkout's digest beside the real one).
docs/specs/pala-1/consistency-vectors.json -text
docs/interop/scitt-statement-vector.json -text
docs/interop/scitt-statement-vector-v3.json -text
# Generated files the tests compare byte-for-byte with a fresh build: LF in
# every checkout, so a Windows runner's autocrlf cannot make them stale.
site/**/*.html eol=lf
site/**/*.xml eol=lf
site/**/*.txt eol=lf
integrations/COMPATIBILITY.md eol=lf
